## ISS-012: `throw new Exception` in audit hash chain verification

### File
`/root/Redball/src/Redball.Core/Security/SecurityAuditService.cs`

### Original
```csharp
                    var entry = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<AuditEntry>(line);
                    if (entry == null) throw new Exception("Invalid JSON formatting");
```

### Replacement
```csharp
                    var entry = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<AuditEntry>(line);
                    if (entry == null) throw new InvalidDataException("Invalid JSON formatting in audit log");
```

### Reason
Uses `InvalidDataException` (or a custom audit exception) instead of the base `Exception`, improving exception classification and caller handling.

### Verification
`dotnet build src/Redball.Core/Redball.Core.csproj`
